WEBVTT

NOTE Timing is estimated from script and acoustic pauses; listening review pending.

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.135
Decision-ready messages usually
fail in predictable ways.

00:00:04.135 --> 00:00:07.930
The sender repeats facts without
explaining the implication.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:12.865
Background comes before the conclusion.

00:00:12.865 --> 00:00:16.595
Words such as “high,” “late,” or
“many” appear without comparison.

00:00:16.595 --> 00:00:19.560
A problem arrives with
no recommendation.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.595
The action is “monitor closely.”

00:00:22.595 --> 00:00:25.100
No owner or deadline is named.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.825
Each failure has a repair question.

00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:31.475
So what does that mean? Compared
with what, and by how much?

00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:35.820
What would you recommend
if it were your decision?

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.245
Who does what, and by when?

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:42.385
Would removing this fact
change the decision?

00:00:42.385 --> 00:00:44.905
Editing is not just shortening.

00:00:44.905 --> 00:00:49.795
It is testing whether each sentence
moves the audience toward responsible

00:00:49.795 --> 00:00:50.240
action.
